      <!--

    ************************ PointViewer ************************

    A lone Point is a map pin, not a disc: a head, a tip pointing down, a white eye, and an
    invisible frame so the pin is a marker in the box rather than the box itself. The editor picks
    the viewer registered for the most specific type, so this wins over GeometryViewer.
-->
      <!--
        MapLayerViewer: HDE.WidgetsAndViewers.vl LayerViewer (vvvv 7.4), copied verbatim with three values
        changed - FixAspectRatio Reference Size 1,1 to 4,3; Scale 2,2 to 8/3,2; Scale (Uniform) 1.05 to 1.
        LayerViewer squares the bounds it gets and shows that square in its 4:3 widget, leaving the
        strips left and right empty (the maintainer asked why, 2026-11-08); this one fits the bounds
        at 4:3 and fills the widget. GeometryViewer gives it a 4:3 frame (ViewFrame).
      -->
